# proof.pattern — Describe your zero-knowledge proof here
#
# Format:
#   Secret <Type> Inputs: (<name1>, <name2>, ...)
#   Public <Type> Inputs: (<name1>, <name2>, ...)
#   Constants:
#       <name>  # description
#   compute: <name> = <expression>
#   check: <lhs> == <rhs>
#
# Types: Int, G1, G2, Fq12
#
# Expressions:
#   e(A, B)       — BLS12-381 pairing (G1, G2 → Fq12)
#   [scalar]point — scalar multiplication
#   A + B         — point addition
#   H(x)          — MiMC hash (works on any type — Int, Fq12, G1)
#   q^a           — exponentiation (shorthand for [a]q)
#   x * y         — field multiplication
#   x >= y        — range comparison (expensive in-circuit)
#
# Example (hash preimage):
#
#   Secret Int Inputs: (x)
#   Public Int Inputs: (y)
#   compute: h = H(x)
#   check: y == h
#
# More examples in example/ — see peace-protocol.pattern, schnorr-knowledge.pattern, etc.
#
# After writing your proof, prompt Claude:
#   "Generate the circuit from proof.pattern"
#
# Then run: ./run
